{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790445907387,"sessionID":"ses_f211bc3baffeg6LamG3HSZFNNY","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"read_4_691995d6","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/task_config.json"},"output":"<path>/workspace/task_config.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"instruction\": \"Add a Camera2D node centered on the playfield, attach a Camera2D.gd script that stores displacement, velocity, and the SPRING=900, DAMP=18, MULTIPLIER=20 constants, and implement a shake(right_pointed) method that reverses direction based on who scored. Update pong.gd so new_ball() keeps respawning the Ball and also calls Camera2D.shake() after every score. In _physics_process(), apply spring-damper physics to update velocity and displacement, then set position.x = displacement to drive the horizontal spring motion.\"\n3: }\n\n(End of file - total 3 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"instruction\": \"Add a Camera2D node centered on the playfield, attach a Camera2D.gd script that stores displacement, velocity, and the SPRING=900, DAMP=18, MULTIPLIER=20 constants, and implement a shake(right_pointed) method that reverses direction based on who scored. Update pong.gd so new_ball() keeps respawning the Ball and also calls Camera2D.shake() after every score. In _physics_process(), apply spring-damper physics to update velocity and displacement, then set position.x = displacement to drive the horizontal spring motion.\"\n}","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/task_config.json","text":"{\n  \"instruction\": \"Add a Camera2D node centered on the playfield, attach a Camera2D.gd script that stores displacement, velocity, and the SPRING=900, DAMP=18, MULTIPLIER=20 constants, and implement a shake(right_pointed) method that reverses direction based on who scored. Update pong.gd so new_ball() keeps respawning the Ball and also calls Camera2D.shake() after every score. In _physics_process